of arsenic contaminated groundwater in alluvial aquifers
from Delta Plains, Eastern India: options for safe drinking
water supply. Int. J. Water Resour. Manag. 13, 79–82.
Ghosh, D., Routh, J., Därio, M. & Bhadury, P. 2015. Elemental and biomarker characteristics in a Pleistocene aquifer
vulnerable to arsenic contamination in the Bengal Delta
Plain, India. Appl. Geochem. 61:87–98.
Ghosh, D., Routh, J. & Bhadury, P. 2017. Sub-surface biogeochemical characteristics and its effect on arsenic cycling
in the Holocene grey sand aquifers of the Lower Bengal
Basin. Front. Environ. Sci. 5:82.
Shrivastava, A., Ghosh, D., Dash, A. & Bose, S. 2015. Arsenic
Contamination in Soil and Sediment in India: Sources,
Effects, and Remediation. Curr. Pollution Rep.: 35–46.
Kabata-Pendias, A. & Pendias, H. 1989. Trace elements in
soils and plants; CRC Press: Boca Raton, FL.
Usman, A.R.A., Alkredaa, R.S. & Al-Wabel, M.I. 2013.
